From: Emre Yavuzalp <emreyavuzalp@gmail.com>
Subject: econet-eth: PPE search-miss FORWARD instead of FORWARD_BUILD

FORWARD_BUILD(3) makes the hardware auto-learn and auto-bind FOE entries for
every flow it sees without the driver building them. Those entries carry no
valid L2/L3/VLAN rewrite data (observed: bind=43 with ipv6-6rd/ipv4-dslite
garbage shortly after boot) and can mis-forward routed traffic.

Switch to FORWARD(2): on a miss the engine punts to CPU with UN_HIT and the
real hash slot in the QDMA descriptor, where en75_ppe_offload_rx_commit()
publishes driver-built entries. Expected TB_CFG changes from 0x14fbc to
0x14fac (SEARCH_MISS bits 5:4 = 2).
--- a/econet_ppe.c
+++ b/econet_ppe.c
@@ -274,13 +274,13 @@ void en75_ppe_start(struct en75_ppe *ppe)
 	      EN75_PPE_TB_CFG_AGE_TCP |
 	      EN75_PPE_TB_CFG_AGE_UDP |
 	      EN75_PPE_TB_CFG_AGE_TCP_FIN |
-	      /* FORWARD_BUILD: the engine learns each flow at its real hash
-	       * slot (reported via crsn HIT_UNBIND/RATE_REACHED) - the only
-	       * slot it actually searches. The plain-FORWARD miss slot is not
-	       * on that set. (Auto-bind garbage is the cost; addressed next.)
+	      /* FORWARD: on a search miss the engine punts to CPU (UN_HIT)
+	       * with the real hash slot in the descriptor. Driver-built entries
+	       * are committed there via en75_ppe_offload_rx_commit(). No
+	       * hardware auto-learn (FORWARD_BUILD self-populates garbage).
 	       */
 	      FIELD_PREP(EN75_PPE_TB_CFG_SEARCH_MISS,
-			 EN75_PPE_SEARCH_MISS_ACTION_FORWARD_BUILD) |
+			 EN75_PPE_SEARCH_MISS_ACTION_FORWARD) |
 	      FIELD_PREP(EN75_PPE_TB_CFG_KEEPALIVE,
 			 EN75_PPE_KEEPALIVE_DISABLE) |
 	      FIELD_PREP(EN75_PPE_TB_CFG_HASH_MODE, 1) |
--- a/econet_qdma.c
+++ b/econet_qdma.c
@@ -206,9 +206,9 @@ static void en75_qdma_rx_process_one(struct en75_q_rx *q, u32 cpu_i,
 	switch (get_erx_crsn(&desc.msg.erx)) {
-	case 0x0d:	/* UN_HIT */
+	case 0x0d:	/* UN_HIT: under FORWARD the hardware reports the real
+			 * hash slot on a miss; publish any staged entry. */
 	case 0x0e:	/* HIT_UNBIND */
-	case 0x0f:	/* HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED: under FORWARD_BUILD these carry
-			 * the engine's real learned slot; publish the staged entry. */
+	case 0x0f:	/* HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED */
 		en75_ppe_offload_rx_commit(en75_eth_ppe(q->qdma->eth), skb, hash);
 		break;
 	case 0x16: {	/* HIT_BIND_FORCE_CPU: a bound entry was hit. Log once
 			 * so the offload path can be confirmed on hardware. */
